From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Camo Tim <camolottim@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: x1p42100-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge-15: Add
 the Elan touchpad

The tree describes one touchpad: the Zinitix part at 0x40 on i2c13, with
its HID descriptor at 0xe. Samsung fits other touchpads in this chassis.
The NP750XQB has an Elan part on the same bus and interrupt (TLMM 3) at
0x15, with its HID descriptor at 0x1. Nothing answers at 0x40 there, so
i2c_hid_of never binds and no touchpad appears.

Add a node for the Elan part, on the same interrupt and pinctrl state as
the existing one. A node whose part isn't fitted fails its probe. The
other touchpads Samsung fits aren't described.
---
 .../qcom/x1p42100-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge-15.dts   | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge-15.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge-15.dts
index 993a96b..60d7254 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge-15.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge-15.dts
@@ -914,6 +914,18 @@
 
 	status = "okay";
 
+	/* Elan touchpad, as in the NP750XQB */
+	touchpad@15 {
+		compatible = "hid-over-i2c";
+		reg = <0x15>;
+
+		hid-descr-addr = <0x1>;
+		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 3 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&tpad_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+	};
+
 	touchpad@40 {
 		compatible = "hid-over-i2c";
 		reg = <0x40>;
-- 
2.43.0

